== 6.8 Chapter 6 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Growth in a living organism is best defined as],
  [any change in the shape of the body],
  [an increase in the amount of water in the body],
  [a permanent and irreversible increase in size or mass],
  [an increase in the number of body parts only]
)

#mcq(2, [Development differs from growth in that development],
  [is always accompanied by an increase in mass],
  [involves the appearance of new structures and functions],
  [can only occur in plants],
  [stops at birth]
)

#mcq(3, [Which measurement is most suitable for following the growth of a seedling?],
  [Height of the shoot only],
  [Dry mass],
  [The colour of the leaves],
  [Fresh mass]
)

#mcq(4, [A sigmoid growth curve is characteristic of],
  [an insect with an exoskeleton],
  [a human being],
  [a crystal forming in solution],
  [a moulting cockroach]
)

#mcq(5, [The growth curve of an insect is stepped because],
  [insects stop growing after the first moult],
  [the rigid exoskeleton must be shed before growth can continue],
  [insects grow only during the rainy season],
  [insects have no cells in their exoskeleton]
)

#mcq(6, [The shedding of the exoskeleton by an insect is called],
  [ecdysis],
  [regeneration],
  [germination],
  [metamorphosis]
)

#mcq(7, [The second rapid phase of growth in a human being occurs],
  [in old age],
  [before birth],
  [at adolescence],
  [during infancy]
)

#mcq(8, [Growth in a human being stops because],
  [the bones become hollow],
  [the pituitary stops making all hormones],
  [the muscles can no longer stretch],
  [the growth plates at the ends of the long bones fuse]
)

#mcq(9, [Which of the following is a complete metamorphosis?],
  [Butterfly: egg, larva, pupa, adult],
  [Cockroach: egg, nymph, adult],
  [Grasshopper: egg, nymph, adult],
  [Termite: egg, nymph, adult]
)

#mcq(10, [The stage of complete metamorphosis in which the insect is inactive and does not feed is the],
  [egg],
  [larva],
  [pupa],
  [adult]
)

#mcq(11, [A nymph differs from a larva in that a nymph],
  [has a pupal stage before it becomes an adult],
  [always lives in water],
  [never feeds],
  [resembles a small adult and has no pupal stage]
)

#mcq(12, [One advantage of complete metamorphosis is that],
  [the young and the adult never compete for the same food],
  [the insect produces more eggs than it can carry],
  [the insect grows continuously without moulting],
  [the insect becomes warm-blooded]
)

#mcq(13, [The larval stage of the mosquito can be controlled by],
  [draining or oiling stagnant water],
  [planting more trees],
  [spraying the adult with insecticide only],
  [feeding the larvae]
)

#mcq(14, [Which of the following is an example of incomplete metamorphosis?],
  [Housefly],
  [Bee],
  [Grasshopper],
  [Moth]
)

#mcq(15, [Secondary sexual characters in the human male are produced mainly by],
  [oestrogen],
  [testosterone],
  [insulin],
  [thyroxine]
)

#mcq(16, [The growth spurt at puberty in both sexes is driven by growth hormone together with],
  [insulin and glucagon],
  [adrenaline and noradrenaline],
  [ADH and aldosterone],
  [the sex hormones]
)

#mcq(17, [Which change occurs at puberty in girls but not in boys?],
  [Beginning of the menstrual cycle],
  [Increase in muscle mass],
  [Deepening of the voice],
  [Growth of pubic hair]
)

#mcq(18, [Puberty in a human being is triggered by hormones from the],
  [pancreas],
  [adrenal medulla],
  [pituitary gland],
  [thyroid gland]
)

#mcq(19, [The stage of human development between fertilisation and about eight weeks is called the],
  [infant],
  [foetus],
  [embryo],
  [zygote]
)

#mcq(20, [Which of the following is not a stage in the development of a human being?],
  [Nymph],
  [Embryo],
  [Zygote],
  [Foetus]
)

#mcq(21, [Two seedlings are grown, one in the dark and one in the light. After a week the dark-grown seedling is taller. This shows that],
  [the light-grown seedling is dead],
  [increase in height alone is not a reliable measure of growth],
  [light prevents growth],
  [the dark seedling has grown more in dry mass]
)

#mcq(22, [An insect that moults five times passes through],
  [four nymphal stages and one adult],
  [five larval stages],
  [no growth at all],
  [a pupa after every moult]
)

#mcq(23, [The term 'adolescence' is best described as],
  [the period of social and emotional change between childhood and adulthood],
  [the period from birth to two years],
  [old age],
  [the moment of fertilisation]
)

#mcq(24, [Which of these is not a secondary sexual character?],
  [Growth of a beard in boys],
  [Production of sperm in boys],
  [Breast development in girls],
  [Broadening of the hips in girls]
)

#mcq(25, [In a growth curve, the plateau at the top indicates that],
  [the measurement was wrong],
  [the organism is still a juvenile],
  [growth has stopped],
  [the organism is dead]
)

#mcq(26, [Which of the following organisms would be expected to show discontinuous growth?],
  [Cockroach],
  [Maize plant],
  [Human being],
  [Cow]
)

#mcq(27, [Measurement of growth by dry mass requires],
  [weighing the plant while it is fresh],
  [measuring the height of the plant],
  [counting the leaves],
  [drying the plant to constant mass before weighing]
)

#mcq(28, [A tadpole develops legs and loses its tail as it becomes a frog. This is an example of],
  [excretion],
  [growth only],
  [reproduction],
  [development]
)

#mcq(29, [The main hormone that controls overall body growth in a child is],
  [oestrogen],
  [insulin],
  [adrenaline],
  [growth hormone from the pituitary]
)

#mcq(30, [Too little growth hormone in childhood results in],
  [goitre],
  [acromegaly],
  [dwarfism],
  [gigantism]
)

